  "task": "X38 h=4 exact toral-line classifier",
  "theorem": "Let psi(X)=X^4+a3X^3+a2X^2+a1X+a0 over odd characteristic. If psi(lambda X)=psi(X) for lambda != 1, then lambda^4=1. For m=ord(lambda), every nonzero coefficient has exponent divisible by m; hence m is 2 or 4 and psi=Phi(X^m), a cyclic pullback. No exact inverse toral line XY=c divides psi(X)-psi(Y), since X^4(psi(X)-psi(c/X)) has nonzero X^8 coefficient. Therefore a primitive h=4 quartic two-fiber residue has no exact toral line."
